<BaseLayout title="About — Bilgenur Pala" description="How Bilgenur Pala approaches backend AI engineering and evidence-led development.">
  <section class="page-intro shell section-space">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>I learned the system before asking the model to act on it.</h1>
    <p>I moved from PHP and MySQL into Python, FastAPI, data-backed APIs, authentication, and containerized services. Agent engineering is the next layer, not a replacement for that foundation.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell about-grid">
    <div class="about-main">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>I use AI as a mentor and collaborator. It helps me compare options, question assumptions, and inspect weak reasoning. I keep the decisions, implementation, and verification with me because those are the parts I need to defend.</p>
      <p>When something breaks, I do not edit the story into a clean success. I record the failure, change one thing, and verify again. The build log matters because the path to a result is part of the engineering evidence.</p>
      <p>I prefer a narrow system with visible limits over a broad claim I cannot test. That is why SafeBump upgrades one direct dependency at a time, requires approval before remote actions, and never describes passing tests as complete safety.</p>
